        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. 'US military leverage a risky tactic': Bombs, military escalation will not bring Iran 'to the table' Middle East Issued on: 20/04/2026 - 14:05 Genie Godula is pleased to welcome Jim Townsend, Adjunct Senior Fellow in the CNAS Transatlantic Security Program and former Deputy Assistant Secretary of Defense (DASD) for European and NATO Policy. According to Townsend, US–Iran negotiations are shaped by tactical manoeuvering: a pre-negotiation ritual in which both sides position themselves strategically through public posturing and calculated obstruction. Ultimately, meaningful progress will depend on mediation, incremental trust-building, and the extension of fragile ceasefires. Trump sending US delegation for Iran talks in Pakistan 19/04/2026 Middle East 'Ceasefire in the Middle East, especially in Lebanon, are meant to be broken', analyst says 19/04/2026 Middle East Iran asserts leverage in Hormuz ahead of new round of talks 19/04/2026 Middle East Israel's double game between negotiations with Lebanon and occupation in the south 19/04/2026 Middle East Food security under threat as Middle East war disrupts fertiliser supply 19/04/2026 Middle East A petition called 'Lebanon will not be the next Gaza' calls on French leaders to take action 19/04/2026 Middle East Iran: Prolonged conflict reshapes view of the regime, analyst says 19/04/2026 Middle East Middle East: Hezbollah blamed after French peacekeeper killed in Lebanon 19/04/2026 Middle East What is UNIFIL? the UN mission in southern Lebanon explained 19/04/2026 Middle East"
